# shots_break.pdl - breaking a block, shot so the viewer SEES it: a two-high pillar of dirt, the crack after one swing, the pillar one block shorter with the dropped block floating after the break, then the pickup (idle = the driver's expiry). Harness rows (verb:); shots_break_human.pdl is the same with keys.
SETUP | spawn 142 100
SEAT | harness
SHOT | k01-face   | harness | verb:face e  | 143 100 3 3.2 250 -10 | 2 | 300 | Asa faces east
SHOT | k02-place1 | harness | verb:place   | 143 100 3 3.2 250 -10 | 2 | 300 | Place a dirt block in front of her
SHOT | k03-place2 | harness | verb:place   | 143 100 3 3.4 250 -8  | 2 | 300 | Place a second one on top: a pillar two blocks high
SHOT | k04-swing1 | harness | verb:mine    | 143 100 4 3.4 250 -8  | 3 | 250 | First swing: cracks open on the top block
SHOT | k05-break  | harness | verb:mine    | 143 100 4 3.4 250 -8  | 4 | 300 | Second swing: it breaks. The pillar is one block lower and the block drops as a small item
SHOT | k06-collect| harness | idle         | 143 100 3 3.4 250 -8  | 3 | 300 | The item flies into the bag: collected
